  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_031 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) achieved the best validation accuracy (0.678) so far, only modestly above the RNA-only scvi_n200 multiprofile avgpool baseline (config_005, 0.650). Image-only models are very weak (~0.21–0.23), so it is unclear how much the image branch is truly contributing versus adding noise. The only multimodal fusion tested so far is 'weighted'; we have no evidence on whether 'concat' fusion would perform comparably or differently. Question: config_030 is identical to config_031 except fusion=concat, giving a clean single-variable A/B test of the fusion strategy. Why this is the best next experiment: Under a limited budget, isolating one design choice (fusion method) at the current best-performing configuration maximizes information gain. If concat ≈ weighted, the fusion choice is not a bottleneck and we can pivot to testing image encoder quality (ViT-L) or aggregation. If concat is substantially worse, we confirm weighted fusion is critical and should lock it in before exploring other axes. This avoids confounding multiple changes and directly informs whether the modest multimodal gain over RNA-only is robust to fusion design."
}

